From 8de24b3d4cab59d6b8c879d7c03a4ccc99408bdb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Antonio D'Achille <existenz70@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 12:08:37 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 08/10] Ming-Image 0.1 Design-Layer: layer decomposition in the
 engine (learned padding, frames, zero-caption guidance)

Design-Layer decomposes the input picture into RGBA layers: it denoises the recomposed picture and
the N layers together as N+1 frames of one sequence, the picture as a clean reference frame after
them. In the engine the batch is the frames (batch size = layers + 1, as Qwen Image Layered).

- ModelImporter: a Z-Image-named DiT with pad tokens is Ming-Image when the safetensors metadata
  says image_model ming_image (ComfyUI's repack); x_pad_token / cap_pad_token are written; 711 or
  713 tensors.
- ZImage / LoRAZImage: `frames` target frames per sample (input batch = batchSize * frames),
  embedded one after the other and read out the same way.
- MingImageFixed: `capPadLength` learned caption padding (cap_pad_token after the caption).
- UNetFixedEncoder (.mingImage): Layer when the DiT has the pad tokens: learned padding for the
  caption and the image, frames = batch size, guidance against an all-zero caption of the same
  length (the reference's negative), captions side by side as Z-Image's guidance path expects.
  Design is unchanged (zero-masked padding, no guidance).
- UNetProtocol: frames = latents' batch / caption's batch for Ming-Image.
- TextEncoder: the negative's length is the caption's (the all-zero caption).
- ModelConverter --ming-connector-only: only the connector, proj_in/out, DirectVLM projection and
  query tokens (Layer shares Design's language model and vision tower).
- MingDiTTest: MING_FRAMES / MING_LEARNED against ref_dit_layer.py.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
